# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the FFmpeg tests (used by the thread-sanitizer preset only).
# FFmpeg's shared libraries are not instrumented: libavcodec's slice and frame threads synchronize
# their own buffers with primitives ThreadSanitizer cannot see (atomics and progress flags in the
# uninstrumented code), so the only accesses it sees from them are the intercepted calls (memset,
# memcpy, malloc and free inside libavcodec and libavutil), and valid decoding is reported as races
# between FFmpeg's threads and with the dvv code that reads a decoded frame after FFmpeg has handed
# it over.
# called_from_lib: makes ThreadSanitizer skip every intercepted call made from code inside the
# named library (a substring of the loaded file's path, e.g. libavcodec.so.62): its memory accesses
# and its synchronization (mutexes, condition variables, semaphores). Thread creation and join stay
# visible. Unlike race:, it does not hide races in dvv code on memory FFmpeg allocated or on threads
# FFmpeg created, so dvv code that FFmpeg's threads run (today the dvv log callback) stays checked.
# - A race between dvv code and an FFmpeg access stays hidden (seen without suppressions: the
#   copyAndPublish memcpy against an av_buffer_allocz memset on a frame thread, a hand-over through
#   FFmpeg's atomics). dvv_components.ffmpeg_single_thread checks the container path without
#   suppressions.
# - FFmpeg's locks are invisible: a callback that FFmpeg's threads run must synchronize with dvv
#   threads through dvv primitives (atomics or dvv mutexes), or it is reported as a race.
# - ThreadSanitizer aborts the process when a matched library is unloaded or one entry matches two
#   loaded files: a test that uses this file must not reach the loader's paths that close FFmpeg
#   libraries again (a partial, refused or lavfi-incomplete FFmpeg build).
# With this list the FFmpeg suites report nothing, so no race: entry is needed.
called_from_lib:libavutil.so
called_from_lib:libavcodec.so
called_from_lib:libavformat.so
called_from_lib:libswscale.so
called_from_lib:libswresample.so
called_from_lib:libavfilter.so
